It has always seemed unfair that the only way to get experience in NH is
to kill things.  I would _really_ like to see priests gain experience
from turning undead, wizards get some points for successfully casting
a spell, rogues from picking locks... and maybe also special incentives
for fighting with the weapon type appropriate to the character's class.

NetHack is a great game, but I really think it is unbalanced in the area
of experience points.  Furthermore, it makes it difficult to give a
character any kind of personality when it is advantageous for all
characters to just wear plate mail and lug a big sword.  The only
character I ever ascended was a big, stupid Barbarian with a good sword
and 250 HP.


